      </table>

      <h2>How Round-Robin WhatsApp Rotation Works</h2>
      <p>Round-robin distribution is an algorithmic method of cycling through a list of resources sequentially. When applied to WhatsApp click-to-chat links:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Prospect #1</strong> clicks your link &rarr; Directed to <em>Agent 1 (Sarah)</em></li>
        <li><strong>Prospect #2</strong> clicks your link &rarr; Directed to <em>Agent 2 (Michael)</em></li>
        <li><strong>Prospect #3</strong> clicks your link &rarr; Directed to <em>Agent 3 (Priya)</em></li>
        <li><strong>Prospect #4</strong> clicks your link &rarr; Loops back to <em>Agent 1 (Sarah)</em></li>
      </ol>
      <p>Every rep gets an equal share of opportunities, response times drop to under 60 seconds, and no lead gets left unread in a queue.</p>

      <h2>Step-by-Step Setup: Creating a Multi-Number Link with LinkWA</h2>
      <p>Setting up your team rotator takes less than a minute:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Go to the <a href="/#multi-number">LinkWA Multi Number Tool</a>.</li>
        <li>Select your country code and enter your first agent's WhatsApp phone number.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>+ Add Number</strong> to add secondary and tertiary numbers for your team members.</li>
        <li>Enter your pre-filled inquiry text (e.g. <em>"Hi, I would like to book a consultation for the premium plan."</em>).</li>
        <li>Optionally add a team tag or agent identifier in the prompt so your CRM or spreadsheet can log the source.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Generate Multi-Number Link</strong>.</li>
        <li>Copy your unique short link (e.g., <code>https://linkwa.in/p/xyz123</code>) and place it on your landing pages, bio links, or ads.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Best Practices for Managing a Multi-Agent WhatsApp Team</h2>

      <h3>1. Track Individual Agent Attribution</h3>
      <p>If you pay commissions based on deals closed, you need to know which agent handled the first touch. You can append an agent code to the pre-filled template message, or teach agents to label new leads with their name tag in WhatsApp Business Labels (e.g., "Sarah - Follow Up").</p>

      <h3>2. Use Pre-Saved Quick Replies</h3>
      <p>Equip every team member with standardized WhatsApp Business Quick Replies (shortcuts using <code>/</code>). When a customer taps the rotator link, every agent should be able to send an identical, professionally formatted greeting and product catalogue within 30 seconds.</p>

      <h3>3. Rotate Shifts Dynamically</h3>
      <p>If Agent 2 is on leave or working a night shift, simply update your active list in LinkWA to redistribute inbound clicks among only the active reps on duty.</p>

      <h2>Who Benefits Most from Multi-Number Rotation?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Real Estate Agencies:</strong> Distribute property inquiries across 5–10 licensed agents without a central call center operator.</li>
        <li><strong>Performance Marketing Teams:</strong> Drive heavy Facebook & Google Ads traffic to WhatsApp without triggering account rate limits on a single phone.</li>
        <li><strong>E-Commerce & High-Ticket D2C:</strong> Allow dedicated product specialists to answer sizing, material, and custom order questions in real time.</li>
        <li><strong>Coaching & Consulting Firms:</strong> Route students to academic advisors or admissions coordinators based on live availability.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>Does the customer see the other agents' phone numbers?</h3>
      <p>No. When a prospect clicks the rotator link, they are routed exclusively to the single agent assigned for that turn. They only see that specific phone number in their chat screen.</p>

      <h3>Can I use landline numbers?</h3>
      <p>Only if the landline has been registered as a verified WhatsApp Business account capable of receiving WhatsApp messages.</p>

      <h3>Is there any limit to the number of clicks a rotator link can handle?</h3>
      <p>No. LinkWA's infrastructure is built on high-performance global edge networks capable of routing tens of thousands of simultaneous clicks with zero latency.</p>

